    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d569">

                <pb facs="0786" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.60 a 11/1</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs of San
                        Marino</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gozi</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation<anchor n="1" xml:id="d569-f1"
                    />]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Marino</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic">February 2,
                        1924</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received February 20.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">984/A/XLI</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to inform Your
                    Excellency that the distinguished Commander Ignazio Pollak, Envoy Extraordinary
                    of the Republic of San Marino to foreign parts and more particularly to the
                    territories of the States of Germany and Austria, has been appointed for all of
                    the current year 1924 to be also Envoy Extraordinary to the States of North
                    America, where there is not at present any consular office in the service of
                    this Government.</p>
                <p>The above-named Commander Ignazio Pollak will present himself to Your Excellency
                    to deliver the greetings of the Government and people of San Marino, the
                    smallest but the oldest state of the world, who have always had good grounds to
                    trust in the sincere friendship of the great people of the United States.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gozi</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
